From f5b54893cbc15b9c3b06856bb11ab13082360a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:18:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Eden (Doris): GPU fences wait for what the GPU wrote
 (setting, on by default); report passes reopened on the same targets;
 bad-overlap notes sampled

- New Doris setting "GPU fences" (doris_fence_wait, default 1). With GPU Fence Behavior
  "Immediate" (or "Default" below High GPU accuracy) Eden releases every fence to the game as
  soon as the GPU emulation thread records it. The build 22 report: about 4500 fences every 10
  seconds in TotK, 2500 of them released while bytes the GPU wrote into buffers before them were
  still to be copied back (about 15 MiB a second), so the game read what was there before. With
  the setting on, such fences behave as "Balanced": released once the GPU has run the work and
  the copy has landed, in order; fences with nothing to copy back still go at once. 0 keeps
  GPU Fence Behavior as it is.
- Report: render passes begun on the same targets as the one that just ended, per frame.
- Pairs of textures kept apart are described 1 in 8 (up to 9000 every 10 seconds).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
