     <string name="doris_texture_cleanup_description">How old textures are removed from GPU memory. Eden copies each texture the GPU drew into back to game memory and waits for the GPU every time (a hitch), and below 1.6 GB of GPU memory keeps those drawings while removing everything else after 50 frames, so TotK keeps re-uploading textures. Doris copies back without waiting, removes a texture only after its copy is done (and keeps it if it was used meanwhile), and gives every texture 300 frames below 2.45 GB. Takes effect right away.</string>
     <string name="doris_texture_cleanup_doris">Doris: no waits, fewer re-uploads</string>
     <string name="doris_texture_cleanup_eden">Eden (as before)</string>
+    <string name="doris_fence_wait">GPU fences</string>
+    <string name="doris_fence_wait_description">When the game is told the GPU has finished its work. With GPU Fence Behavior set to Immediate (or Default below High GPU accuracy), Eden tells it as soon as the work is recorded, before the GPU has run it and before what the GPU wrote is back in game memory, so the game reads old data until the copy lands. Doris waits for the copy, like Balanced (fences with nothing to copy back still go at once). Takes effect right away.</string>
+    <string name="doris_fence_wait_doris">Doris: wait for what the GPU wrote (default)</string>
+    <string name="doris_fence_wait_eden">As GPU Fence Behavior says</string>
     <string name="doris_gpu_barriers">GPU barriers</string>
     <string name="doris_gpu_barriers_description">How the game\'s \"wait until the GPU is done\" points are carried out. Eden\'s way lets later drawing read results that aren\'t finished yet on Adreno, which can make distant terrain, buildings and shadows drop out for a frame. Doris uses real barriers; by default only where something drawn since the previous wait needs one (most of the game\'s waits follow nothing of the kind), which spares the GPU work. Takes effect the next time the game starts.</string>
     <string name="doris_barriers_eden">Eden (as before)</string>
